# ./bootstrap.sh inputs. Copy this file to .env.bootstrap and fill in the FIVE
# values below -- that is everything a first-time install needs. How to obtain
# them (a Databricks service principal + an AWS key pair) is in docs/BOOTSTRAP.md.
# .gitignore excludes .env.* so your filled-in copy can never be committed.

# 1. Databricks workspace URL
DATABRICKS_HOST=https://dbc-00000000-0000.cloud.databricks.com

# 2. Databricks service principal client id   (OAuth M2M -- not a personal access token)
DATABRICKS_CLIENT_ID=replace-me

# 3. Databricks service principal secret       (OAuth M2M -- not a personal access token)
DATABRICKS_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-me

# 4. AWS access key id    (a permanent IAM user; starts with AKIA)
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=replace-me

# 5. AWS secret access key
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=replace-me

# =============================================================================
#  YOU CAN STOP HERE. Fill the five values above and run ./bootstrap.sh.
#
#  Everything else is OPTIONAL and derived for you -- the SQL warehouse, the AWS
#  region, the Unity and Delta catalogs, an alternate env-file. Don't worry
#  about any of it: bootstrap works it out and tells you, before spending
#  anything, if it ever needs your help. There is no sixth required value. To
#  pin one anyway, see docs/BOOTSTRAP.md; the full variable reference (for the
#  manual ./antidemo path, not a starting point) is .env.example.
# =============================================================================
